From fdbee2941ab50ad350de2bd861d0c6fb7d594a09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:46:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban fence: exempt the fenced root's auto-pruned
 scratch dir, so probe homes stop leaking in ~

Kanban scratch-home probes made a throwaway HERMES_HOME with `mktemp -d ~/kanban-probe.XXXX` (the
SCRATCH_HOME_HINT route), because the env-inherited fence covers the whole marker root (~/.hermes),
TMPDIR included. The route's recursive delete of "$H" is approval-blocked in unattended Kanban runs,
so the homes stayed: 7 homes, ~4.8 GB on 4 pool workers at 2026-11-13 06:40Z (t_01a1d3b5bfc898e7).
The only automatic temp cleanup, the 24 h idle scratch pruner, covers only <home>/cache/scratch.

- agent/delegation_context.kanban_path_is_fenced: for an env-inherited path marker, a target that
  resolves (symlinks first) strictly under <marker root>/cache/scratch (get_scratch_dir(root), the
  worker's TMPDIR) is not fenced. The scratch dir itself, the pinned HERMES_KANBAN_DB, the legacy "1"
  marker and in-process delegate children stay fenced. The scratch path is not resolved, so a scratch
  dir that symlinks elsewhere under the root exempts nothing. The tool fence's HERMES_HOME check
  (tools/kanban_tools_fence._env_fence_covers_board) and the CLI's go through the same predicate.
- SCRATCH_HOME_HINT: H=$(mktemp -d "$TMPDIR/kanban-probe.XXXX"); unset the board pins; the scratch
  pruner removes the home after 24 h idle (deleting it is optional where allowed).
- History: the "not TMPDIR" wording came with cdf04b9d0b (the scratch-home route) only because the
  fence covered the whole root; no reason to exclude the scratch dir is recorded.
- The fence stays cooperative scoping, not confinement: a hardlink into scratch bypasses it the same
  way a hardlink into ~ already did.

Tests (tests/tools/test_kanban_tools_scratch_home_fence.py): a scratch-dir home reaches real logic
in-process (tool and DB fence) and in a real owner-bound worker subprocess; homes under root/sub,
root/cache/other and root/cache, a board elsewhere under the root, a symlink in scratch to a board
under the root, a scratch dir symlinked into the root, a pinned DB under scratch, the legacy marker
and an in-process delegate child stay refused; the local-writes-only scope holds for a scratch-dir
home; the refusal names the new route; prune_scratch_dir(max_idle_hours=0) removes an idle
kanban-probe.* home with its board. test_kanban_fenced_missing_board moves its fenced fixture board
from root/cache/scratch to root/sub.

Proof: on origin/main 5ad0bdcf60 the new tests fail 6 (route text x2, scratch-dir in-process, local
scope, predicate, subprocess); with the change 24/24 pass; 95 fence/delegation files 1960 passed.
Mutants (6/6 killed): scratch dir itself exempt, no exemption, scratch resolved, pinned check
dropped, target not resolved, scratch=cache.
